      "body": "## Problem\n\nThe CUDA image build fails at the `framework` stage with:\n\n```\nerror: No solution found when resolving dependencies\n  runai-model-streamer[s3]>=0.15.7 and pandas==3.1.0 are incompatible\n```\n\n### Root cause\n\nThe `torch_deps` stage freezes the fully-resolved dependency set into `constraints.txt`:\n\n```dockerfile\nuv pip freeze | grep -vE \"^sglang( |==|@)\" > /sgl-workspace/constraints.txt\n```\n\n`python-dateutil` has just released **3.0.0**, so it is captured as the latest and frozen as `python-dateutil==3.0.0` (pandas 3.1.0 only requires `python-dateutil>=2.9.0`, so nothing actually needs 3.0.0).\n\nThe `framework` stage then runs:\n\n```dockerfile\nuv pip install -c /sgl-workspace/constraints.txt ... pandas ... \"runai-model-streamer[s3,gcs,azure]>=0.15.7\"\n```\n\nThe `[s3]` extra pulls `runai-model-streamer-s3 -> boto3 -> botocore`, and **botocore requires `python-dateutil<3.0.0,>=2.1`**. The hard `==3.0.0` pin from the freeze collides with that, so the resolution is unsatisfiable.\n\n## Fix\n\nRelax the frozen `python-dateutil` pin to `<3.0.0` right after generating `constraints.txt`, so later stages can resolve a compatible 2.9.x that satisfies both `pandas` (`>=2.9.0`) and the boto3/botocore chain (`<3.0.0`).\n\n## Verification\n\nReproduced and verified with `uv pip compile` (platform `x86_64-manylinux_2_34`, Python 3.12), using the frozen pins plus a realistic boto3 floor:\n\n| constraints | result |\n|---|---|\n| `python-dateutil==3.0.0` | `No solution found` (reproduces the failure) |\n| `python-dateutil<3.0.0` | **Resolved** → `python-dateutil==2.9.0.post0`, `boto3`/`botocore==1.43.117`, `pandas==3.1.0` |\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #39827073974](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39827073974)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39827073739](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39827073739)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:heavy_minus_sign: **No AMD PR run found for this commit**.<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
