  "files": [
    {
      "additions": 6,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/56c31b8adfdd5fdae2476c3fbaab9599866339da/docker%2FDockerfile",
      "changes": 7,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/contents/docker%2FDockerfile?ref=56c31b8adfdd5fdae2476c3fbaab9599866339da",
      "deletions": 1,
      "filename": "docker/Dockerfile",
      "patch": "@@ -212,6 +212,10 @@ COPY rust/sglang-api-types /tmp/sglang_deps/rust/sglang-api-types\n \n # Install sglang dependencies (torch, transformers, etc.).\n # Generate constraints.txt to prevent reinstalling these deps in later stages.\n+# Relax the python-dateutil pin captured by the freeze above: the newly\n+# released python-dateutil 3.0.0 gets frozen as the latest (pandas only\n+# needs >=2.9.0), but boto3/botocore pulled by runai-model-streamer[s3]\n+# require python-dateutil<3.0.0, making the later install unresolvable.\n RUN --mount=type=cache,target=/root/.cache/uv \\\n     --mount=type=cache,target=/root/.cargo/registry \\\n     case \"$CUDA_VERSION\" in \\\n@@ -228,7 +232,8 @@ RUN --mount=type=cache,target=/root/.cache/uv \\\n         --index-strategy unsafe-best-match \".[${BUILD_TYPE}]\" \\\n     && cd /sgl-workspace \\\n     && rm -rf /tmp/sglang_deps \\\n-    && uv pip freeze | grep -vE \"^sglang( |==|@)\" > /sgl-workspace/constraints.txt\n+    && uv pip freeze | grep -vE \"^sglang( |==|@)\" > /sgl-workspace/constraints.txt \\\n+    && sed -i 's/^python-dateutil==.*/python-dateutil<3.0.0/' /sgl-workspace/constraints.txt\n \n # Cosmos3 guardrails default ON: sglang enables them whenever `cosmos_guardrail`\n # is importable (Cosmos3Pipeline.create_pipeline_stages); opt out at runtime with",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/raw/56c31b8adfdd5fdae2476c3fbaab9599866339da/docker%2FDockerfile",
      "sha": "164a480a09f4abb01f2aea52550eafee9f0ec691",
      "status": "modified"
    }
  ],
  "inline_comments": [],
  "issue_comments": [
    {
      "body": "Hi maintainers — gentle ping for a review and the `run-ci` label so the gated CI can run.\n\nThis is a small one-line Dockerfile fix for a currently-broken CUDA image build: the `torch_deps` freeze now captures the freshly-released `python-dateutil==3.0.0`, which then collides with `botocore` (pulled via `runai-model-streamer[s3]`, requires `python-dateutil<3.0.0`) in the `framework` stage, making the install unresolvable (`No solution found`). The fix relaxes just that frozen pin to `<3.0.0`; verified with `uv pip compile` (details + before/after table in the PR description).\n\n@mmangkad you touched the uv/constraints flow in #42612 — would appreciate your eyes here. Thanks!\n",
      "created_at": "2026-10-22T18:00:52Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/45860#issuecomment-6347652148",
      "id": 6347652148,
